.TH "CRUFT" "1" "September 2026" "cruft" "cruft User Manual"
.SH NAME
.PP
cruft \- Calculinux reduced footprint framebuffer terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.B cruft
.RB [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B cruft
is a Linux framebuffer terminal emulator derived from yaft, tuned for
low memory on Calculinux devices.
.PP
The alternate screen buffer (DECALT) is implemented, so full-screen
programs (vim, htop, less) run on their own buffer and leave the main
screen intact when they exit.
.PP
When a status font is installed, cruft draws a status bar in the margin
strip above the cell grid: the clock in the centre, and a wifi signal
stair and battery indicator on the right. A segment whose data source is
absent (bare hardware, VM) is hidden; a missing or unsuitable status
font disables the bar entirely and the grid reclaims the full screen.
.PP
Lines that scroll off the top of the main screen are kept in a
scrollback ring (see
.BR CRUFT_HISTORY ).
While any history is stored, a thin scrollbar in the right edge of the
grid shows the current position; full-screen programs run on the
alternate screen and never pollute the history.
.SH KEYBOARD
.PP
History navigation keys (all require the Meta/Alt modifier; the bare
arrows remain readline's):
.RS
.TP
Meta-Up / Meta-Down
one line deeper into / out of the history
.TP
Meta-Prior / Meta-Next
half a page (Prior: deeper; Next: towards the live screen)
.TP
Meta-Home / Meta-End
oldest stored row / live tail
.RE
.PP
Any other key while browsing scrolls back to the live tail and is
delivered to the program. Sequences are matched only at the start of a
keypress, so a split-delivery ESC will occasionally pass through.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.PP
Rewrite conf.h before make.
The default status bar segment selection (used when
.B CRUFT_SB
is unset) is the
.B sb_default_segments
conf.h variable (default "all").
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B FRAMEBUFFER
Specify framebuffer device (default /dev/fb0).
.TP
.B CRUFT_FONT
Path to a CRUFTFN1 font blob (default /usr/share/cruft/console.cruftfont).
.TP
.B CRUFT
If this variable includes "wall", cruft enables wallpaper mode and a
framebuffer shadow buffer. See cruft_wall.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB
Status bar segments: a comma-separated list of
.B time ,
.B wifi
and
.BR battery ,
or
.B all
(the default) to show every segment whose source is present,
.B none
(or
.BR 0 )
to disable the bar. Unknown names are ignored with a warning.
.TP
.B CRUFT_HISTORY
Scrollback depth in rows (default 96, capped at 1024).
0 disables the ring and the scrollbar. Stored rows carry copied cell
contents; sixel pixmaps in history are deep-copied up to a 64 KiB
budget, oldest art degrading to blank beyond it.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB_12H
Set to 1 for a 12-hour clock (\fIH:MMam/pm\fP); the default is
24-hour.
.TP
.B CRUFT_SB_FONT
Path to the 4x8 CRUFTFN1 status font
(default /usr/share/cruft/status.cruftfont, installed by the
miniwi-console package).
